[
    {
        "content": "<p>When there is a non definitional equality where the LHS or RHS occurs underneath a cast I am not able to rewrite it. I can close it using grind but simp fails</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myDef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">42</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myDef_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myDef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- We cast from (MyType n) back to (MyType 0)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- so that the result is a Bool, matching the Right Hand Side.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">congrArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">myDef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">myDef</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  n : Nat</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  h : 0 = n</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  ⊢ cast ⋯</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">      (match n with</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">      | 0 =&gt; true</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">      | n.succ =&gt; 42) =</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">    true</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  -/</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592488069,
        "sender_full_name": "Frederick Pu",
        "timestamp": 1777758663
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this is not because it occurs under a cast, but because you are trying to rewrite at a dependent position</p>",
        "id": 592488725,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1777759245
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But the simp works without the cast tho</p>",
        "id": 592493482,
        "sender_full_name": "Frederick Pu",
        "timestamp": 1777763441
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can you provide an <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> of it working without the cast?<br>\nAlso, if you <code>import Mathlib</code> you can <code>rw! [← h]</code></p>",
        "id": 592495525,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777765453
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(deleted)</p>",
        "id": 592495532,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777765457
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What is rw!</p>",
        "id": 592495561,
        "sender_full_name": "Frederick Pu",
        "timestamp": 1777765493
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's hard to help you if you don't put effort. Try my suggestion and you can use \"go to definition\" on <code>rw!</code> to read more about it, or look it up in the docs</p>",
        "id": 592495872,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777765964
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i dont really see why this magically fixes the issue tho: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">`rw!` is like `rewrite!`, but also cleans up introduced refl-casts after every substitution.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">It is available as an ordinary tactic and a `conv` tactic.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592496084,
        "sender_full_name": "Frederick Pu",
        "timestamp": 1777766238
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>cause rw gives an error that it cant find an occurence of the pattern</p>",
        "id": 592496101,
        "sender_full_name": "Frederick Pu",
        "timestamp": 1777766258
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>which is a misleading error message</p>",
        "id": 592496108,
        "sender_full_name": "Frederick Pu",
        "timestamp": 1777766270
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"676310\">Frederick Pu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Unable.20to.20perform.20rw.20or.20simp.20under.20cast/near/592496108\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>which is a misleading error message</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Indeed, but that's a separate problem- <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"270676\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Error.20messages.20suggestions/with/579493810\">#lean4 &gt; Error messages suggestions</a></p>",
        "id": 592497292,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777766687
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>with just the match simp is able to close: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mySimpleMatch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mySimpleMatch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">mySimpleMatch</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592498205,
        "sender_full_name": "Frederick Pu",
        "timestamp": 1777766856
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>so the issue is from the cast</p>",
        "id": 592498253,
        "sender_full_name": "Frederick Pu",
        "timestamp": 1777766864
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"676310\">Frederick Pu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Unable.20to.20perform.20rw.20or.20simp.20under.20cast/near/592498253\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>so the issue is from the cast</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yes but the underlying issue is what <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> said. See <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Error.20messages.20suggestions/near/564797014\">#lean4 &gt; Error messages suggestions @ 💬</a> for an explanation.<br>\nBasically, the <code>cast</code> call contains a proof about <code>n</code>, so you can't change <code>n</code> to <code>0</code> because the proof depends on <code>n</code>.</p>",
        "id": 592499021,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777767006
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's an example without <code>cast</code> which fails, again because stuff depend on <code>n</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mySimpleMatch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mySimpleMatch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">mySimpleMatch</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592499978,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777767180
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"933054\">Snir Broshi</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Unable.20to.20perform.20rw.20or.20simp.20under.20cast/near/592499021\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yes but the underlying issue is what <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> said. See <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/Error.20messages.20suggestions/near/564797014\">#lean4 &gt; Error messages suggestions @ 💬</a> for an explanation.<br>\nBasically, the <code>cast</code> call contains a proof about <code>n</code>, so you can't change <code>n</code> to <code>0</code> because the proof depends on <code>n</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This is something that <code>simp</code> can actually get around, since it can cast the proof.</p>\n<p>The actual issue is that the <code>n</code> in <code>match n with | 0 =&gt; true | n + 1 =&gt; 42</code> is in a dependent position, since if you make a function out of it the type of the function is <code>(n : Nat) -&gt; MyType n</code>, which is a dependent arrow, the return type depends on the argument. When rewriting stuff like that <code>simp</code> can only use <code>dsimp</code> theorems, since otherwise the result may be not type correct.</p>",
        "id": 592503338,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1777767845
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Unable.20to.20perform.20rw.20or.20simp.20under.20cast/near/592503338\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This is something that <code>simp</code> can actually get around, since it can cast the proof.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Can you show an example?</p>",
        "id": 592504537,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1777768653
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>here's how you can get around having the dependent type in your goal by wrapping it in a <code>let</code> which also happens to be an example of <code>simp</code> casting a proof</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- We cast from (MyType n) back to (MyType 0)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- so that the result is a Bool, matching the Right Hand Side.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">congrArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">myDef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bool</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">cast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">congrArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MyType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hk</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">myDef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 592504753,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1777768822
    }
]